source	Plato, Gorgias 474c-475c, tr. B. Jowett
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 1672, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1672
class	equivocation
word	evil
fault	what is fine is measured by its pleasure or benefit to those who see or meet it, so what is more disgraceful exceeds in pain or harm to someone; that it is the greater evil for the one who does it is another sense of "evil"
reference	G. Vlastos, "Was Polus Refuted?", American Journal of Philology 88 (1967)
